{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413487-cool-stuff-in-your-world","id":1413487,"title":"Cool Stuff in Your World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-13T20:54:14-07:00","id":1413487,"title":"Cool Stuff in Your World","content":"The World presented in Scion 2E is really cool concept wise, but it leaves a lot open for the Storyteller to create. So I was wondering what are some of the cool things that you have created for your version of the World, be it a place, building, event, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I'll post mine below<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The town of Pantheon, WI has a big weekend long festival to kick off the tourist town's summer season and to give thanks to the Gods for the start of their most prosperous season. The festiveal is called <i>Wicker Mania</i> due to the long held town tradition of creating figures from wicker (or other flammable materials) and burning them in tribute to the Gods. This simple task has evolved quite a lot over the years, to the point where a contest is held and prizes are given out for more elaborate wicker figurines. Last year a local high school student made a glorious depiction of the Teotl god Quetzelcoatl, complete with multicolored corn husks to represent the Feathered Serpent's glorious plumage. Of course, all contestants must burn their creations before the end of the weekend, but not before several pictures are taken of the finalists. The festival is also host to several tents for selling crafts (wicker furniture is, of course, popular) as well as a carnival for the younger kids.. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:56:00-07:00","id":1414304,"title":"","content":"I like to think of a Scion/Denizen equivalent of Callahan's Crosstime Saloon. Complete with the fireplace and the tradition of toasting and then hurling the glasses into the fire, for &quot;to absent friends&quot; toasts to Scions who've fallen... And, perhaps, also those who've ascended to Godhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 09-17-2020, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}